.venv
.crush
*.pyc
results.json
.coverage
.vscode
.python-version
.env
.vite
# e2e endpoint file: same reason as `.env` — it names a machine-local server and
# may hold its key. The committed template is `.env.test.example`.
.env.test
node_modules
web/dist
.playwright-mcp/
.kilo/plans/
logs/
# e2e scratch folders. They are top-level (not under `logs/`) because the app's
# own rules hide `logs/**` from the Editor, and the specs need a scratch the
# pane can actually see and write.
/e2e-write/
/e2e-ws-root/
/e2e-modes-root/
mcp_connectors/externals.json
# The workspace policy folder: machine-local per checkout, and the app reserves
# it (hidden and unwritable from the Editor), so it is never source. The LSP
# declaration (.nojae/lsp-settings.json) and its seeded template live here too,
# and may carry secrets in their per-entry `env` maps.
.nojae/
resources/memory_registration.json
pyrightconfig.json
# Upstream font drops (a full Nerd Fonts family is hundreds of MB). The build
# consumes only the woff2 subsets generated from them into web/src/fonts/, and
# those ARE committed as build inputs; the originals are re-downloadable, so
# they stay out of git. The leading slash anchors this to the repo root so it
# does not also catch web/src/fonts/ (which must stay tracked).
/fonts/